    {
      "id": "p0134-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Normally, a food item disappears after being used, but the Bisicle becomes the \"Unisicle\" after one use. As we can see, there's wordplay at work here: the two item names sound like the words \"bicycle\" and \"unicycle'', while also sounding like the word \"popsicle\".",
        "raw": "Normally, a food item disappears after being used, but the Bisicle becomes the\n\"Unisicle\" after one use. As we can see, there's wordplay at work here: the two\nitem names sound like the words \"bicycle\" and \"unicycle'', while also sounding\nlike the word \"popsicle\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28860785,
          0.31085,
          0.90412511,
          0.37877857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28656836,
          0.31013571,
          0.91104917,
          0.37985
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          23,
          24,
          25,
          26
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "食物一般用过就会消失，Bisicle 吃过一次却会变成“Unisicle”。这两个名称既像 bicycle（自行车）与 unicycle（独轮车），也像 popsicle（冰棒）。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
