    {
      "id": "p0134-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This wordplay would be lost in a literal translation into Japanese, so the translator compensated by referring to a different, but similar Japanese ice cream treat known as \"Papico\". Papico packages generally contain two plastic, ice cream-filled bottles. And just like double popsicles, they're designed to be broken apart and eaten separately or shared with someone else.",
        "raw": "This wordplay would be lost in a literal translation into Japanese, so the\ntranslator compensated by referring to a different, but similar Japanese ice\ncream treat known as \"Papico\". Papico packages generally contain two plastic,\nice cream-filled bottles. And just like double popsicles, they're designed to be\nbroken apart and eaten separately or shared with someone else.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2955421,
          0.57675714,
          0.89951587,
          0.66227857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28656836,
          0.57604286,
          0.91104917,
          0.66335
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          37,
          38,
          39,
          40,
          41
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "直译会让日语失去这个文字游戏，因此译者换成了一种不同却相似的日本冰品：Papico。每包 Papico 有两个装着冰淇淋的塑料瓶，和双头冰棒一样，可以掰开分别吃，也可以分给别人。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
